"""
dashboard.py
------------
Filing-centric lineage engine + Streamlit UI + visual export.

This is the counterpart to bridge.py. All the COM/Excel automation has
been moved OUT of this file and into bridge.py, which runs as its own
process and listens on localhost. This file:
  - traces lineage (formula / named range / fuzzy fallback),
  - classifies nodes and assembles the lineage dict,
  - runs the Streamlit UI,
  - builds the exported vis-network HTML diagram, whose side-panel
    "Open in Excel" buttons fetch() against the bridge instead of calling
    any Python function directly (there is no live Python behind a
    file:// page -- see bridge.py's docstring for why).

On "Open Visual in New Tab", this file:
  1. writes the uploaded workbook to a stable temp path on disk (once
     per uploaded file, not once per click -- reused across the session),
  2. makes sure a bridge.py subprocess is running and reachable,
  3. bakes that file path + the bridge's port into the exported HTML so
     its JS knows where to send locate requests and for which file.

Run with:
    streamlit run dashboard.py
"""

